WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:05.550
I don’t know if this is our Marco Rubio
moment…

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.750
Certainly I don't think it's necessary to
question the President's motives.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:13.900
But really I think it's fair to question his
judgment, because he's made the decision that

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.100
U.S. policy has to change in order for Cuba
to change.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.660
The reality is anybody that understands or
really cares much about Cuba recognizes the

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.380
problem is the regime.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:30.910
The President has scuttled a policy that's
been based on pre-conditions for normal economic

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:32.279
and political change.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:33.690
Free labor unions.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.320
Some sort of commitment to holding elections.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:39.300
Giving people their basic human rights.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:45.560
Cuba is the only country in the Western hemisphere
that cannot meet any of those conditions.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:51.489
And I think the President must recognize that
the Cuban people, 11 million Cubans, will

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:55.829
pay the price if the regime feels that it
can act with impunity.

00:00:55.829 --> 00:01:00.149
The President can salvage this if he really
insists on fundamental change.

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:05.070
Up to now, he has been pouring on concessions
and getting very little in return.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.060
That has to change.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:09.329
What do you think about the President’s
trip to Havana?

00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:13.110
Please offer your comments and give us ideas
about topics you’d like us to cover in the

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:13.119
future.

